  "content": "<p><strong>Instructor:</strong> Dennis Freeman</p>\n<p><strong>Description:</strong> Discrete-time systems can be represented in several ways: difference equations, block diagrams, and operators. Each method requires a different analytical approach. Feedback loops in cyclic systems lead to convergent or divergent responses.</p>\n",
